# Schema Review Against Acceptance Criteria

Purpose: review whether the database design and current backend implementation can support the detailed acceptance criteria for sensory-aware route planning, congestion avoidance, sensory refuges, and predictive alerts.

## Current Implementation Context

The team has confirmed MySQL/Aiven as the shared database platform. There are currently two schema paths in the repository:

- `database/schema.sql`: a planned MySQL logical schema.
- `backend/app/models/*`: SQLAlchemy models used by the running backend and ingestion scripts.

For local integration testing, the backend models have been used as the operational source of truth because the route-planning API, ingestion scripts, and frontend are already written against those model names and columns. A separate Aiven database, `escape_ellie_test`, was used for safe testing so the team database `escape_db` was not overwritten.

